{"id": "EUVD-2026-103922", "enisaUuid": "55af6d9a-f831-36cd-909d-b30c93ed51ae", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: buffer: Ensure bounce buffer used for unaligned case is zeroed.\n\niio_push_to_buffers_with_ts_unaligned() leaks uninitialized heap memory\nto userspace if the data passed in is not a multiple of 8 bytes and the\ntimestamp is enabled. Specify __GFP_ZERO for the devm_krealloc()\nto ensure any extra space is cleared.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:44:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:32", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b4f53cec8cc94b37601ce0bb2b272b6753beed98", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5c2f21f645e40c70fda2a4283e6f2a81e5cb9f2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b134ef820610bd873c9d59999d9824710964ce82", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a87212b1a09a1fdd730ce5520f7b1fc0b488511", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5330036bc68d23672bfcc16c60c54701ae123083"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98668", "GHSA-f4c5-jpx2-jvrg"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2cbf1ef3-6564-3cc5-8f6f-a739f53792d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "3790a928-28ff-3857-800a-269b8a5a35f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "385d454b-437f-3b13-8deb-b23373636c04", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "95ec3fdf2b79eaff79e78688bbc2f7dbb98d68b6 <5330036bc68d23672bfcc16c60c54701ae123083"}, {"id": "3d103d8c-f4e4-3e30-b46f-0eda2b96b705", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "95ec3fdf2b79eaff79e78688bbc2f7dbb98d68b6 <b5c2f21f645e40c70fda2a4283e6f2a81e5cb9f2"}, {"id": "3ded43e2-2a80-3f1b-9b40-5737d0cc2d86", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "95ec3fdf2b79eaff79e78688bbc2f7dbb98d68b6 <3a87212b1a09a1fdd730ce5520f7b1fc0b